{"tool_name":"centiserver","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"centiserver","home":"http://www.centiserver.org/","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"CentiServer is a comprehensive online resource that provides over 110 definitions of different centrality indices, their computational methods, and algorithms in the form of an encyclopedia. In addition, CentiServer allows users to calculate 55 centralities with the help of an interactive web-based application tool and provides a numerical result as a comma separated value (csv) file format or a mapped graphical format as a graph modeling language (GML) file.","addition_date":"2018-10-14T20:17:39Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:59:01Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library","Web application"],"version":["1.0.0"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:centiserver","credit":[{"email":"alimgh@ams.ac.ir","name":"Mahdi Jalili","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/centiserve/centiserve.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Statistical calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2238"}]}],"name":"CentiServer","operating_system":["Mac","Windows"],"owner":"daniel_stefan","publication":[{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0143111","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2015 Jalili et al.This is an open access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original author and source are credited.Various disciplines are trying to solve one of the most noteworthy queries and broadly used concepts in biology, essentiality. Centrality is a primary index and a promising method for identifying essential nodes, particularly in biological networks. The newly created CentiServer is a comprehensive online resource that provides over 110 definitions of different centrality indices, their computational methods, and algorithms in the form of an encyclopedia. In addition, CentiServer allows users to calculate 55 centralities with the help of an interactive web-based application tool and provides a numerical result as a comma separated value (csv) file format or a mapped graphical format as a graph modeling language (GML) file. The standalone version of this application has been developed in the form of an R package. The web-based application (CentiServer) and R package (centiserve) are freely available at http://www.centiserver.org.","authors":[{"name":"Alimoghaddam K."},{"name":"Arab S.S."},{"name":"Asgari Y."},{"name":"Ghavamzadeh A."},{"name":"Jalili M."},{"name":"Salehzadeh-Yazdi A."},{"name":"Yaghmaie M."}],"citationCount":37,"date":"2015-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"PLoS ONE","title":"CentiServer: A comprehensive resource, web-based application and R package for centrality analysis"},"pmcid":"PMC4646361","pmid":"26571275","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Applied mathematics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3569"},{"term":"Data integration and warehousing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3366"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"CentiServer","home":"https://bio.tools/centiserver","license":"GPL-3.0","version":"1.0.0","summary":"CentiServer is a comprehensive online resource that provides over 110 definitions of different centrality indices, their computational methods, and algorithms in the form of an encyclopedia. In addition, CentiServer allows users to calculate 55 centralities with the help of an interactive web-based application tool and provides a numerical result as a comma separated value (csv) file format or a mapped graphical format as a graph modeling language (GML) file.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:centiserver:1.0.0/cmd/www.centiserver.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/license